  "format": "salts maps a name to base64 of 32 bytes. Each case: recordName = prefix + \"_\" + base32lower(HMAC-SHA256(key: the 32 decoded salt bytes, message: UTF8(type + \"\\n\" + id)))[0..<26]; base32 is RFC 4648, lowercase, no padding. ZoneRoot is always named root. saltIDs gives each salt's id: the first 8 hex characters of sha256 of the 32 decoded salt bytes (§2.4 step 6). Ids compare exactly: an uppercase UUID names a different record from its lowercase form. idFrom, when present, is how the id itself is derived (§4.1): SittingLegacyID = \"sit:legacy:\" + the first 24 hex characters of sha256(UTF8(input)), input session:<session_id> or day:<YYYY-MM-DD>; SourceFileID = SourceIdentity.fileID(input) = \"src_\" + hex(sha256(UTF8(\"source:v1:file:\" + input))), input the 64 lowercase hex characters of the file's sha256 (D47). SourceURLID = \"src_\" + hex(sha256(UTF8(\"source:v1:\" + input))), input a URLNormalizer v1 key (SourceIdentity.stableID). CollectionID = \"col_\" + hex(sha256(UTF8(\"collection:v1:\" + input))), input <kind>:<externalKey>. A migrated quiz score's Sitting uses SittingLegacyID with input quiz:<courseQuiz|lectureQuiz>:<preference key> (§4.1, revision 3). Satellite ids use revision 6's roles: legacyBase.<shard> with shard 00–3f, seedManifestDelta.<deviceID>.<passID>, moveMap.<moveJobID>.<pass> and moveMap.folded.<n> on the personal root, and a notebook's cover; a \"Recovered:\" Doc is recovered:<artifactID>:<hash>, the hash of the body it saves (§4.1, §3.5.30).",
